      "content": "At 35<sup>o</sup>C, the vapour pressure of CS<sub>2</sub>\n is 512 mm. Hg and that of acetone is 344 mm Hg. A solution\nof CS<sub>2</sub>\n in acetone has a total vapour pressure of 600 mm Hg. The false statement amongst the\nfollowing is :",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "CS<sub>2</sub> and acetone are less attracted to each other than to themselves."
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "a mixture of 100 ml. CS<sub>2</sub> and 100 ml. acetone has a volume &lt; 200 ml."
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "Heat must be absorved in order to produce the solution 35<sup>o</sup>C"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "Raoult's law is not obeyed by this system."
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "B"
      ],
